<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila call loan rates jump for 3rd straight day.</title>
<headline>Manila call loan rates jump for 3rd straight day.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>----------------------- Nov 6 ---------------------------</p>
<p>* Central Bank maintains lending rate at 15 percent</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Manila overnight money soared for the third straight day to an average of 14 percent on Wednesday from 12.28125 as banks continued to borrow funds to cover their four-day weekend positions, traders said.</p>
<p>&quot;Big banks were borrowers today. I believe they held off from borrowing early in the week thinking that rates would ease later,&quot; said a foreign bank dealer.</p>
<p>&quot;It backfired on them,&quot; another said.</p>
</text>
